<title>GREECE: Greek WPI inflation falls to 6.2 pct y/y in Aug.</title>
<headline>Greek WPI inflation falls to 6.2 pct y/y in Aug.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's wholesale price inflation fell to 6.2 percent year-on-year in August from 6.4 percent in July and 6.6 percent in the same month in 1995, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said in a statement.</p>
<p>The WPI index firmed 0.2 percent month-on-month in August after dropping 0.6 percent month-on-month in July and rising 0.4 percent in August 1995, it said.  </p>
<p>    Wholesale Price Index   Aug 96   Jul 96   Aug 95</p>
<p>    Month/month (pct)	   0.2    -0.6	0.4</p>
<p>    Year/year (pct)	     6.2     6.4	6.6</p>
<p>    Index (1980=100)	  847.6   846.1     798.3</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
